# Do not over-engineer

## Scope

- Fix the reported problem; do not refactor adjacent modules
- One ADR-worthy decision per change — do not bundle unrelated improvements
- No generic "utils" folders for one-liners used once

## Abstractions to avoid

- Repository/DAO layers above `orbitypeSql()` — the client is already thin
- Plugin registries beyond filename-based `import.meta.glob`
- Config-driven section maps duplicating the filesystem registry
- Wrapper components that only pass props through unchanged

## Features

- Do not add revalidation, comments, or email providers until env and schema support them
- Do not introduce ISR, Redis, or edge middleware to "future-proof" caching — ADR-0005 chose native CDN cache
- Do not add content collections unless the project opts in (out of template scope)

## Tests

- Write e2e tests for behaviour users depend on — not for implementation details
- Do not mock Orbitype in unit tests when seed/mock mode already covers dev flows

When in doubt, ship the smaller diff and document the extension point.
